<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43488" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēmĭ-hŏmo</span></b> ,
			ĭnis, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a half-man</i>, i. e. <i>half man and half beast.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Centauri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 536</span></i>
			 (for which, semiferi, <i><span class="en">id. ib. 12,
				406</span></i> al.; v. semifer, I.): mandragoras (because formed
			below like a man), Col. poët. 10,
			19.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>half-human</i>, i.
			e. <i>half-wild</i>, <i>half-savage</i>,
			= semifer, II.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cacus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 194</span></i>
			 (for which, semifer, <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8,
			267</span></i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nasamones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					11, 180</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
